    "created_at": "2022-07-25T12:11:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-25T12:11:03Z",
    "body": "> Note that on Android there is an open issue preventing Chrome from receiving advertisements from iBeacon devices because we are telling the operating system we aren't interested in location-related devices as that requires requesting a different permission than non-location-related devices.\r\n\r\nOutch, I tried during days and days before reading this answer. \r\nbluetooth-internal didn't show the ibeacon but in my demo using watchAdvertisement I received a truncated (only 7 or 8 bytes of data) event (with the Apple ID in the data) \r\nDo you know how we can bypass this permission ?\r\nthanks ! ",
